We establish a uniform convergence result for an irreducible, positive recurrent Markov chain with countable state space toward its Q-process under the strong topology of bounded continuous functions, utilizing the convergence of tail probabilities at a specific rate. This finding extends a previous theorem by Baccelli and Quianer, which was limited to birth and death chains. Furthermore, we demonstrate that the Q-process of a continuous time Markov chain converges uniformly to the original chain under the same topology, thereby generalizing the work of Baccelli and Quianer. Finally, we apply these findings to analyze the uniform convergence of the Q-processes for the M/M/1 queue and the two-queue system with a shared server. Additionally, we explore the implications of this result for the study of Q-processes.

Keywords: Q-process, tail probability, uniform convergence, strong topology.
